;; =======================================================
;; START-UP CHECKS: THE MACHINE AND ITS MEMORY (AMIGA MODE)
;; =======================================================
;; The game's own check of the machine (MachineProblem{}, sparkydave.machine.ab3): included before the first Dim
;; (the palette data and globals.ab3 come after), so the memory is read before the game takes any. A start from
;; the launcher has had the same check already, in DetectVideo, before the game was loaded: this one is for a
;; start without it. On a 68000 the game's 68020 code would not get this far; that case is the launcher's.
;; The message stays up for a while (about 8 seconds), so a Workbench start's window does not close before it
;; can be read.

machineProblemFound.w = MachineProblem{0}
If machineProblemFound <> #MACHINE_OK
  NPrint MachineProblemText{machineProblemFound, 0}
  VWait 400
  End
EndIf

;; END OF START-UP CHECKS: THE MACHINE AND ITS MEMORY (AMIGA MODE)
